{
  "name": "Budget refresh",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Budget refresh\nScheduled refresh of the household budget.\n\n1. **Fetch** rows from a source (today: statements dropped into the local inbox; later: FinTS).\n2. **Dedup** against the pipeline ledger (Postgres) — every row has a stable key.\n3. **Import** into Actual Budget with a deterministic `imported_id` — re-runs never double-import.\n4. **Summarise** balances, net worth and what happened, and save/post it.\n\nn8n only orchestrates: it calls the pipeline's HTTP API and sees counts, never transactions or credentials.",
        "height": 396,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "note-overview",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -128,
        272
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Sources\nOne HTTP node per source. Add a branch per bank; they all end in *Summary*.",
        "height": 120,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "note-sources",
      "name": "Sources note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        528,
        496
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Idempotent import\n`dedup` partitions rows into new / changed / known using the ledger; `import` writes only new rows to Actual and records them.",
        "height": 140,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "note-import",
      "name": "Import note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1056,
        480
      ]
    },
